# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored: NO ENV FILE IS EVER
# COMMITTED in this repo (owner's rule, 2026-11-15), even though all three
# values below are public by design.
#
# Where the values live:
#   - On a machine: this file's copy, .env (`yarn dev`, `yarn build`).
#   - For the live site: this repo's GitHub Actions VARIABLES, under the
#     same three names (GitHub › stageroll-ltd/stageroll-web › Settings ›
#     Secrets and variables › Actions › Variables tab). The Deploy workflow
#     hands them to `yarn build` and stops if one is missing
#     (.github/workflows/deploy.yml). To change what the live site uses,
#     change the variable there (`gh variable set NAME --body VALUE`) and
#     re-run Deploy; nothing in git changes.
#
# The account pages' Supabase project and Cloudflare Turnstile widget
# (/sign-in/, /productions/). The key is the project's PUBLISHABLE one
# (sb_publishable_…; the name says ANON_KEY because that is what it was,
# and the legacy anon key is retired in early 2027), which reaches only
# what every grant and policy allows the anon role, and a site key only
# names the widget. Never put a secret here or in a GitHub variable:
# anything VITE_ ends up in the page.
#
# Today both the machine and GitHub hold the hosted DEV project's values
# (dlkehqragvyreyyxafnf). Before the account pages go live, GitHub's three
# move to production's (zcdjjfpfkngxwxwhrcgh): its URL, its publishable key
# and its own Turnstile widget ("StageRoll prod", which already lists
# stageroll.co). stageroll-docs #69.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# The account pages themselves are built only with VITE_ACCOUNT_PAGES=on.
# `yarn dev` sets it itself (package.json); nothing sets it for the deploy,
# so the live site has none of them. When billing goes live it becomes a
# fourth GitHub variable, added to the Deploy workflow's build step
# (vite.config.ts, src/account/pages.ts).
